Adapted files (structure/styling kept, data layer rewired from AWX
job_events to the AAP Bridge console API):

- src/components/awx/JobOutput.css
  from frontend/awx/views/jobs/JobOutput/JobOutput.css (verbatim grid,
  plus AAP Bridge additions clearly marked).
- src/components/awx/JobOutputView.tsx
  pattern from JobOutputEvents.tsx + JobOutputRow.tsx (output-grid rows,
  sticky line-number gutter, follow mode). Play/task collapse semantics
  removed: migration consoles are plain text, not Ansible events.
- src/components/awx/JobStatusHeader.tsx
  pattern from JobStatusBar.tsx (title + status baseline, ticking elapsed
  clock). Play/task/host counts replaced with exit-code badges.
- src/components/awx/Ansi.tsx
  original implementation in the spirit of @ansible/common-ui/Ansi
  (MIT `anser` package instead of the monorepo dependency).
- src/components/Layout.tsx (PageHeader helper), JobOutput toolbar and
  app navigation follow AWX PageHeader / JobOutputToolbar conventions.

Per Apache-2.0 §4, this NOTICE and the header comments in each adapted
file preserve attribution. No ansible-ui code outside the presentation
layer is used: no framework packages, routing, i18n, or data fetching.
